{n:'Qualifications & Conditions',s:'Writers limit their claims with conditions and qualifiers. Read them precisely.',t:['Notice words like only, most, may, unless.','A qualifier changes how strong a claim is.'],
 i:[['m','“The vaccine is effective in most adults.” § What does “most” tell you?','It may not work for every adult.','It works for all adults.','It never works.','It works only for children.'],
  ['m','“Students may borrow laptops only during class hours.” § Can a student borrow one at night?','No','Yes','Only on weekends','Only with friends'],
  ['m','“Under certain conditions, the soil can support rice.” § The claim is…','limited by conditions','universal','false','about wheat'],
  ['m','“The policy will reduce traffic, assuming that buses run on time.” § What does the claim depend on?','buses running on time','more cars','new roads','longer workdays'],
  ['m','Which claim is MOST strongly stated?','This method always works.','This method often works.','This method may work.','This method sometimes works.'],
  ['m','“Except for the coastal areas, the region received little rain.” § Where did more rain fall?','the coastal areas','everywhere','the mountains','nowhere'],
  ['m','“The results suggest, but do not prove, a link.” § The writer is being…','cautious','certain','sarcastic','confused'],
  ['m','“Applicants must be at least 16 and have parental consent.” § A 17-year-old without consent…','cannot apply','can apply','must wait a year','needs a teacher'],
  ['m','Why do careful writers qualify claims?','To match the claim to the evidence.','To sound unsure.','To make text longer.','To avoid evidence.'],
  ['m','“In rare cases, side effects occur.” § This means side effects are…','possible but uncommon','common','impossible','guaranteed']],
 w:{p:'Rewrite these overconfident claims so that they are accurately qualified: (1) “Online learning is better than face-to-face learning.” (2) “Exercise cures depression.” (3) “Tourism helps every community.” Explain your changes.',src:'(1) Online learning is better than face-to-face learning. (2) Exercise cures depression. (3) Tourism helps every community.',u:['may|might|can','some|many|most|often|certain'],need:2,k:['online','exercise','tourism'],rewrite:1}},
{n:'Strategic Rereading',s:'When meaning breaks down, reread the right part with a purpose.',t:['Find where you got lost.','Reread to clarify, then continue.'],
 i:[['m','You lose track of who is speaking in a long dialogue. § What should you do?','Reread to find speaker tags and pronoun references.','Skip to the end.','Read faster.','Stop reading.'],
  ['m','A sentence uses an unfamiliar word that seems important. § Best strategy?','Reread the surrounding sentences for context clues.','Ignore it always.','Close the book.','Guess randomly.'],
  ['m','You finished a paragraph but cannot state its main point. § What should you do?','Reread and summarize each sentence briefly.','Move on quickly.','Memorize the paragraph.','Read the next chapter.'],
  ['m','A graph seems to contradict the text. § Best response?','Reread both and check the labels and units.','Assume the graph is wrong.','Ignore the graph.','Ignore the text.'],
  ['m','Which is a sign you should reread?','You cannot explain what you just read.','You understood everything.','The text is short.','The text has pictures.'],
  ['m','You are reading a dense science text. § What pace is best?','slower, with pauses to check understanding','as fast as possible','skimming only','reading backward'],
  ['m','When rereading, what should you focus on?','the specific part that confused you','the whole book again','only the title','page numbers'],
  ['m','A long sentence has many commas. § Helpful strategy?','Break it into chunks and identify the main clause.','Skip it.','Read it louder.','Count the commas.'],
  ['m','Before reading a difficult text, which step helps most?','Preview headings and set a purpose.','Start at the last page.','Read only the pictures.','Read quickly without a purpose.'],
  ['m','After rereading, you still do not understand. § Next step?','Use another resource or ask for help.','Give up.','Pretend you understand.','Delete the text.']],
 w:{p:'Describe a time when you did not understand something you read (a lesson, instructions, or a story). Explain which strategies you used or could have used (rereading, context clues, chunking, summarizing, asking for help) and why they work.',u:['reread','context','chunk','summar','ask|help','preview'],need:3,k:['read','understand']}}
